---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Analytics Disclosure | Varve Docs"
  description="Varve's technical analytics disclosure: the small, consent-gated event inventory and the data Varve never collects."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <article class="analytics-page">
      <h1>Analytics disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The desktop app sends no usage stats. Website and browser-demo analytics record consented
        pageviews, referring site origins, installer-link clicks, demo launches, export formats,
        and demo download clicks using GoatCounter. Unknown consent fails closed. No remote
        tracking script, autocapture, session replay, analytics cookie, or visitor fingerprint is
        used. Unique visitors are not measured; repeated page loads count again.
      </p>

      <h2>Website events</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Fields</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>website_page_viewed</td><td>normalized route</td><td>Understand which documentation and product pages are useful.</td><td>emitted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_download_started</td><td>release, platform, architecture, package type, release channel</td><td>Count installer-link clicks by route and package; not successful downloads or installations.</td><td>sent as website_download_clicked</td></tr>
          <tr><td>browser_demo_launched</td><td>entry source</td><td>Count website clicks into the browser demo.</td><td>sent as demo-launch-website</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_outbound_clicked</td><td>destination category</td><td>Legacy schema category.</td><td>not sent by this website provider</td></tr>
          <tr><td>website_contact_clicked</td><td>channel category</td><td>Legacy schema category.</td><td>not sent by this website provider</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Browser demo events</h2>
      <p>
        The public <code>/try</code> demo uses the same GoatCounter account and the same consent
        key as the website. It sends nothing until the visitor clicks Allow, and nothing when
        Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track is set. The desktop app is not involved.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Fields</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>try page view</td><td>allowlisted <code>ref</code> only</td><td>Count consented demo visits by first-party campaign tag.</td><td>sent as try or try?ref=tag</td></tr>
          <tr><td>demo-launch-direct</td><td>none</td><td>Count a consented demo load, including a mid-session Allow.</td><td>emitted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>demo-export-png / jpeg / webp / svg</td><td>format name only</td><td>Count which export formats the demo is used for.</td><td>emitted</td></tr>
          <tr><td>demo-download-click</td><td>none</td><td>Count clicks on the demo banner Download desktop link.</td><td>emitted</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Desktop events</h2>
      <p>
        Release desktop builds send no usage stats. There is no desktop collector, no usage
        toggle that transmits events, and no leftover product-analytics endpoint. Diagnostics
        telemetry and crash reporting stay on separate controls.
      </p>

      <h2>Never collected</h2>
      <p>
        Documents, canvas pixels, screenshots, exported artwork, clipboard data, filenames, paths,
        project or layer names, user text, comments, URLs from designs, imported metadata, image
        hashes, geometry, generated code, prompts, raw exception strings, raw stacks, device
        identifiers, authentication identities, advertising identifiers, and arbitrary payload
        fields are prohibited by the schema and runtime privacy boundary.
      </p>

      <h2>Consent and transport</h2>
      <p>
        Website and demo consent are stored in
        <code>varve:website-analytics-consent:goatcounter-v1</code>. The client uses a bounded
        in-memory queue, never blocks editing or navigation, and discards pending events when
        consent is revoked or the process ends. The production website and demo deployment maps
        the existing <code>varve.studio</code> switch to the private
        <code>varvestudio.goatcounter.com</code> account. Local and unconfigured website builds
        remain endpoint-free. A new provider-specific consent choice is required; old refusals
        remain respected, and Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track always blocks collection.
        Session identification, individual-pageview storage, and demographic/device collection
        are disabled. Only aggregate counts are retained. Normalized routes omit fragments and
        all query strings except an allowlisted first-party campaign tag; some sections share
        the home category, so that category is not a literal homepage count. Referrers are
        reduced to site origins. Demo event paths never start with a slash.
      </p>
      <p><a href={sitePath('/about/privacy')}>Read the full privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .analytics-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  /* Display typography: the bespoke hero ramp is page art, not a shared role. */
  h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 65ch; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.55; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding: 0.75rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--text-primary); }
  a { color: var(--text-link); }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; } }
</style>
